 "description": "Per-event mass-uncertainty calibration of AN-16-442 5.3.1.  A leg's region is the first region whose |eta| (|eta_SC| for electrons, half-open ranges, null = unbounded) and relative momentum error dpT/pT contain it.  Pairs are binned in the predicted relative mass uncertainty e = 0.5 sqrt(d1^2 + d2^2) (internal edges below; first bin from 0, last bin unbounded).  Each fit is the binned form of the AN conditional fit: all e bins of one pair class fitted simultaneously in the core window (82-100 GeV; the 60-120 window of lambda_v2 misfits the e-sculpted tails) with BW (x) DCB + exponential, DCB tails shared, a free shift, yields and slope per bin, and the DCB sigma of bin k equal to (m_Z / 2) sqrt(lambda_a^2 <d_a^2>_k + lambda_b^2 <d_b^2>_k).  'same': both legs in the target region (AN muons, and ECAL-driven electrons of regions 1 and 3 with their eta subdivisions); 'reference': one leg in the reference region with its lambda fixed from its own fit and the other in the target (the AN method for the electron regions 2 and 4).  Substitution: UL NanoAOD has no ecalDriven flag, so the tracker-driven electron corrections of the AN are not derived separately.",
